@cc [owner:mixxorz,label:architecture] backend-snapshot-authority
Production backend-owned UI state MUST enter the frontend through `app-status-changed` snapshots.
Production snapshot consumers MUST apply a snapshot only when its `stateVersion` is newer than the
latest accepted version; command responses or polling MUST NOT overwrite newer backend state.
Development-only smoke tooling MAY observe snapshots directly for test orchestration.

@cc [owner:mixxorz,label:safety] frontend-safety-is-advisory
Frontend visibility, disabled states, and confirmation controls MAY prevent accidental requests, but
MUST NOT be treated as enforcement of lockout, generation, freshness, or exact-scene safety. Those
decisions MUST remain authoritative in the backend.

@cc [owner:mixxorz,label:product] settings-full-replacement
Each production settings edit request MUST invoke `replace_app_settings` with one complete
`AppSettings` object. Production code MUST NOT send partial settings payloads or treat command
completion as an authoritative projected update. A transient full-object draft MAY be displayed
while awaiting the backend snapshot; tests and stories MAY update mock state locally.
